# Caddy local-service template for Moshpit names
# ----------------------------------------------
#
# Two different jobs, two different servers:
#
#   nginx (this repo, nginx/moshpit-gateway.conf)
#     The SNI-passthrough gateway. It peeks the ClientHello and forwards the
#     TCP stream untouched — it terminates nothing and holds no keys.
#
#   Caddy (this file)
#     The local-service terminator, for names that point AT THIS MACHINE.
#     A moshpit wildcard DNS record (`*.chovy.hacker`) lands every subdomain
#     here, and Caddy serves TLS for each one and reverse-proxies to local
#     ports. This is topology-A-for-localhost: Caddy is a designed-in
#     terminator, which is fine because the "origin" is a process you own,
#     on a loopback socket you own.
#
# `tls internal` is not a shortcut. Public CAs are banned from issuing for
# non-IANA names (CA/Browser Forum Baseline Requirements — issuance stopped
# Nov 2015, stragglers revoked by Oct 2016), so there is no public option to
# choose. Caddy's internal CA is the same trade the proxy's local root makes:
# a CA whose key never leaves this machine. Trust it in your browser once,
# same as ~/.moshpit/ca/ca.crt.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reusable default: internal TLS + fall through to the default local service.
# Import this from any hosted-suffix block.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(moshpit-default) {
	tls internal

	# Default: everything under the suffix goes to localhost:8080.
	# Specific-subdomain overrides belong in `handle` blocks ABOVE this
	# one (Caddy orders `handle` by matcher specificity, so a host match
	# always wins over the catch-all) or in drop-ins under
	# /etc/caddy/moshpit.d/ — see caddy/examples/.
	handle {
		reverse_proxy localhost:8080
	}
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hosted suffix: chovy.hacker
#
# To host another suffix, copy this block and replace every `chovy.hacker`
# (three places: the wildcard, the apex, and any `host` matchers).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.chovy.hacker, chovy.hacker {

	# --- Per-subdomain override (example) -----------------------------------
	# Route one name to a different port than the default. Duplicate this
	# `handle` pair per override, or drop a file in /etc/caddy/moshpit.d/
	# instead of editing this template.
	@app host app.chovy.hacker
	handle @app {
		reverse_proxy localhost:3000
	}
	# ------------------------------------------------------------------------

	# Local services drop their own overrides in /etc/caddy/moshpit.d/*.caddy
	# (see caddy/examples/ in this repo). A glob that matches nothing is a
	# no-op, so the directory may be empty.
	import /etc/caddy/moshpit.d/*.caddy

	# Default route (position doesn't matter — the host-matched handles
	# above outrank it by specificity, but last is the readable place).
	import moshpit-default
}
